  "worked_solution": "First, we factor out $x$ in the expression on the left-hand side.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}5tx-3x & =2 \\\\ x(5t-3) & =2\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we divide both sides by $(5t-3)$ to isolate $x:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x(5t-3) & =2 \\\\ \\frac{x(5t-3)}{5t-3} & =\\frac{2}{5t-3} \\\\ \\frac{x\\cancel{(5t-3)}}{\\cancel{5t-3}} & =\\frac{2}{5t-3} \\\\ x & =\\frac{2}{5t-3}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n**Note:** This result assumes that $5t-3\\ne 0.$",
